; The ".com" TLD zone -- delegates "example.com." to its own authoritative
; server, with in-bailiwick glue (ns1.example.com. lives inside the very
; domain being delegated, so the parent has to ship its address itself).
;
; com.'s own nameserver, a.gtld-servers.cascade., is deliberately named
; *outside* the com. namespace (mirroring real life: a.gtld-servers.net is
; its own separate zone, not part of any TLD it serves) -- its address is
; glue root.zone carries, not something com.zone can hold for itself.
$TTL 3600
$ORIGIN com.
@                         IN  SOA  a.gtld-servers.cascade. hostmaster.gtld-servers.cascade. (
                                   2026081401
                                   3600
                                   900
                                   604800
                                   3600 )
@                         IN  NS   a.gtld-servers.cascade.

example.com.              IN  NS   ns1.example.com.
ns1.example.com.          IN  A    127.0.0.4
